  // clauses like FROM, WHERE, GROUP BY, or ORDER BY. For text-to-SQL, "first
  // complete query" is often not the intended query.
  //
  // This revision changes the stopping rule. We still open the constrained span
  // immediately so the answer is fully SQL-focused, but once inside we no longer
  // close merely because the parser says the prefix is complete. Instead, while
  // there is remaining budget, we keep sampling parser-valid continuations using
  // ConstrainedStep, which can continue a complete prefix into a longer valid
  // query. We only close in two situations: (1) we are at the final available
  // step and the current prefix is complete, so we spend that last step on ">>";
  // or (2) generation has already ended by budget exhaustion, in which case we
  // opportunistically reserve the last step for closing whenever possible.
  //
  // To reduce the chance of short generic queries, the inside policy uses a
  // stronger narrowing heuristic near dead ends and on small valid frontiers:
  // boost top valid candidates, and when the frontier is narrow, scale logits
  // down before strongly boosting valid candidates. This keeps generation on the
  // schema-valid manifold without forcing premature termination. The main fix is
  // therefore strategic rather than cosmetic: defer closure, spend budget on
  // completing the SQL, and only emit the closing delimiter when that is the
  // best use of the remaining step budget.
  // CSD_RATIONALE_END
  // CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
  // parser_validity: In the outside branch, OpenConstrainedSpan enters constrained
  //   mode with currentConstrainedOut := [], and parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by
  //   precondition. In the inside-close branch, we call CloseConstrainedSpan only
  //   when parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) is known, and the helper
  //   exits constrained mode, making the implication vacuous. In the inside-step
  //   branch, all logit adjustments are read-only with respect to the tracked
  //   prefix; the only state-changing append is AppendConstrainedToken applied to
  //   a token returned by ConstrainedStep, so the resulting constrained prefix
  //   remains parser-valid. If next == eosToken, we break without changing the
  //   constrained state, so the invariant is preserved.
  //
  // suffix: In the outside branch, OpenConstrainedSpan appends only the opening
  //   delimiter and sets currentConstrainedOut := [], so the suffix property for
  //   the tracked constrained content holds trivially. In the close branch,
  //   CloseConstrainedSpan appends the closing delimiter and resets the tracked
  //   constrained content to [], so the implication holds immediately. In the
  //   append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same token to generated
  //   and currentConstrainedOut, preserving that currentConstrainedOut is exactly
  //   the suffix of generated of the corresponding length. On eos break there is
  //   no state change, so the invariant remains true.
  //
  // progress: Every non-breaking branch increments steps exactly once. The outside
  //   branch uses one step to append the opening delimiter; the close branch uses
  //   one step to append the closing delimiter; and the inside-step branch uses
  //   one step for a constrained token choice, after which generated either grows
  //   by one via AppendConstrainedToken or stays unchanged on eos break. Thus each
  //   counted step increases |generated| by at most one, preserving
  //   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps.
  // CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
  generated := generatedPrefix;
  insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
  currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
  cost := 0;

  var steps := 0;

  while steps < maxSteps
    invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
    invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
    invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
    invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
    invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
    invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
    invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
    invariant cost == 0
    decreases maxSteps - steps
  {
    if !insideConstrainedOut {
      var openedGenerated, openedInside, openedCurrent := helpers.OpenConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
      generated := openedGenerated;
      insideConstrainedOut := openedInside;
      currentConstrainedOut := openedCurrent;
      steps := steps + 1;
    } else {
      var remaining := maxSteps - steps;
      var complete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
      if remaining == 1 && complete {
        var closedGenerated, closedInside, closedCurrent := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(
          lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut
        );
        generated := closedGenerated;
        insideConstrainedOut := closedInside;
        currentConstrainedOut := closedCurrent;
        steps := steps + 1;
      } else {
